  "scope": "Complete group-start assembly moves to the product adapter while capacity and reservation hooks invoke the original live VM owner. The native journal still validates/commits the complete graph before pending state and visible work. The frozen pre-migration whole VM start independently compares group policy and native state; SQLite fault injection compares every journal table and restart behavior.",
  "limitations": [
    "Preparation invokes trusted capacity and reservation hooks and is not pure. Callers must bound/admit and authorize cold HIR before entry. Already successful reservations remain consumed on later error or unwind.",
    "PreparedGroupStart is public mutable data, not an admission certificate or dispatch grant. Real graph validation, capacity recheck, atomic commit, pending publication, leases and settlement remain native-owned.",
    "The group-start oracle preserves the old whole VM implementation and reuses the previously verified base request builder; it does not prove a second independent implementation of the underlying static request validator.",
    "Root entry coordination, native journal ownership, full host-neutral durable recovery, complete vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. No native maturity promotion is claimed.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no new Linux, GUI or remote CI execution.",
    "The previous standalone checkpoint was reused after rechecking 270 copied sources and 280 exported files. No new standalone export or standalone test run was performed."
